# Keep the build context small and — more importantly — keep secrets and local
# state out of the image. Anything listed here is invisible to `docker build`,
# so it cannot be COPYed in by accident.

node_modules
npm-debug.log*

# Secrets. These must arrive as runtime env vars from the host dashboard,
# never baked into a layer where `docker history` can read them back out.
.env
.env.*
*.pem

# Local database and uploads. Production uses Turso and Cloudinary; shipping a
# stale nook.db would silently shadow them on first boot.
data/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
uploads/

.git
.gitignore
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
